From: Joel Gerber <Jitsusama@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] Split a small free run before carving a large one

A request under 63 slots that found no run of its own size and no room
at the bump pointer took a large run, and split a larger small run only
when no large run was free. The small runs each sweep leaves scattered
stayed free, while every large run carved left the next large request a
new chunk. Over 130 openings in a lab, with the large runs kept by
size, the shell's heap held 25 MB growing to 33 around 18 live. A small
request now splits the smallest larger small run before it looks in
the large bins, and the same lab held 25 MB growing to 29, flat from
its first tenth.

---
--- a/src/qml/memory/qv4mm.cpp
+++ b/src/qml/memory/qv4mm.cpp
@@ -450,6 +450,25 @@
         goto done;
     }
 
+    if (slotsRequired < NumExactBins) {
+        // Split the smallest larger small run before taking a large one, so the scattered
+        // runs of sizes few ask for are used up rather than kept, and the large runs stay
+        // whole for the requests that need them.
+        for (size_t i = slotsRequired + 1; i < NumExactBins; ++i) {
+            m = freeBins[i];
+            if (m) {
+                freeBins[i] = m->freeData.next; // take it out of the list
+                size_t remainingSlots = i - slotsRequired;
+                Q_ASSERT(remainingSlots < NumExactBins);
+                HeapItem *remainder = m + slotsRequired;
+                remainder->freeData.availableSlots = remainingSlots;
+                remainder->freeData.next = freeBins[remainingSlots];
+                freeBins[remainingSlots] = remainder;
+                goto done;
+            }
+        }
+    }
+
     // search the large bins for a large enough item, from the one for this size up. Only the
     // request's own bin holds runs too small for it, and it passes at most a few of them, since
     // each pass of a long list is paid again by every request that follows it; the first run of
